        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for trivy",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for trivy fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-19585: github.com/hashicorp/go-getter: path traversal during S3 and GCS directory downloads may allow files\n  to be written outside the requested destination (bsc#1284829).\n- CVE-2026-78669: golang.org/x/net/http2: excessive CPU consumption from repeated initial window changes (bsc#1285541).\n- CVE-2026-97032: golang.org/x/net/http2: HTTP/2 server crash due to HPACK encoder race (bsc#1287329).\n\nChanges for trivy:\n\n- Update to version 0.76.1:\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
